Tali is the town beneath the surface of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], where the strider's outcasts live: [[Bestiary/Mongrel Folk|mongrel folk]] and others gone far from human shape, bound to the strider's owners and trading in ration slips rather than coin. The followers of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] called the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]] keep to Tali and pass for ordinary townsfolk among them, so that finding one is harder than it sounds.

The town runs from Upper Tali near the surface down into the lower decks. A remedy cellar, the Apothecarium, stands in Upper Tali. The centre of Tali holds the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Chapel of the Six|Chapel of the Six]], and around the dead heart [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Tally|Tally]] lies the quarter of Neweth. A tavern called the Craven Roost rents rooms to the Singers.
